course: dictionary
lesson: 15125
title: Sanguine: hopeful when things are hard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sanguine is a formal word for being cheerful and hopeful, even when things look bad. «Even though it rained all week, Mum was sanguine that the sports day would go ahead.» The clue is «even though it rained all week»: things were hard, but she still expected good things. So sanguine means hopeful, not just happy.
explain: Look for clues in the other words. A sanguine person keeps smiling and believes the next plan will work. Toad in the story is like this: he is always sure his next plan will be a triumph, even after a disaster. If someone is «not very sanguine about our chances», they doubt they will win.
explain: Sanguine is mostly used in news and grown-up talk, not in everyday chat. Some older books also use it to mean rosy or red, as in «a sanguine face» that looks healthy and red. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in "hopeful" for sanguine. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. This works for most uses of sanguine.
fact: Sanguine means cheerful and hopeful about what will happen, even when things are hard.
fact: Sanguine is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in news and grown-up writing.
fact: Old writers used «sanguine» to mean rosy or red, as in a red, healthy-looking face.
fact: In old medicine, doctors thought a person ruled by blood was cheerful. This idea was wrong.
fact: «Sanguine» and «optimistic» both mean hopeful, but sanguine is the more formal word.
exercise: «Even with the rain, Mum was sanguine about the picnic.» What does sanguine mean here? | Worried and afraid | Very tired | Angry and cross | *Hopeful and cheerful
exercise: «Our team is not very sanguine about winning the final.» What does this suggest? | They are very, very hungry | They have already gone home | They expect to win easily | *They are doubtful and not very hopeful
exercise: Find and copy the word that means hopeful and cheerful. «Toad was sanguine that his next plan would work, even after the crash.» | work | *sanguine | crash | plan
test: In old medicine, what were people ruled by blood thought to be? | *Cheerful | Always hungry | Always sleepy | Always cross
test: «The old painting showed a sanguine face, rosy and red.» What does sanguine mean in this sentence? | Cheerful and hopeful | Very thin and pale | Shiny and wet | *Rosy and red
exam: Which sentence uses sanguine correctly? | Sam was sanguine because he had no lunch and was very hungry | Sam was sanguine about the broken bike, which he threw in the bin | *Even after losing the first game, Sam was sanguine that he would win the next one | Sam was sanguine as he sat on the wet pavement, sad and tired
